## Architecture Rules

All rules MANDATORY.

### PHP Standards

- PSR-12, strict types and modern PHP
- Explicit return types with generics: `Collection<int, User>`
- Dependency injection via Laravel's Service Container
- Use Laravel classes over native PHP functions (Filesystem, Process) for testability
- **Yoda conditions:** Always place constants on the left side of comparisons to prevent accidental assignment

### Modern PHP (8.5+)

**Properties:**

- `readonly` properties and classes for immutability
- Property hooks over getter/setter boilerplate
- Asymmetric visibility: `public private(set) string $id`
- Clone with: `clone $obj with { prop: 'value' }`

```php
readonly class UserDTO {
    public string $email {
        set => strtolower(trim($value));
    }
    public private(set) string $id;
}
```

**Types:**

- Enums over class constants for finite values
- Intersection types: `Countable&Iterator`
- DNF types: `(A&B)|null`
- Typed class constants: `public const string NAME = 'foo'`
- Standalone types: `true`, `false`, `null`

**Syntax:**

- `match` over `switch` for value returns
- First-class callables: `$fn = $this->method(...)`
- `new` in initializers: `function foo(Log $log = new NullLog())`
- `new` chaining: `new Foo()->method()`
- Pipe operator: `$val |> trim(...) |> strtoupper(...)`
- Dynamic constant fetch: `MyClass::{$name}`

**Attributes:**

- `#[\Override]` on all overridden methods
- `#[\Deprecated]` for deprecation warnings
- `#[\NoDiscard]` when return value must be used
- `#[\SensitiveParameter]` to redact from stack traces

**Functions:**

- `array_find()`, `array_any()`, `array_all()` over manual loops
- `array_first()`, `array_last()` for element access
- `mb_ucfirst()`, `mb_lcfirst()`, `mb_trim()` for multibyte
- `json_validate()` before decode when validation-only

### PHPStan Type Hints

Use `@var` annotations to help PHPStan understand types it cannot infer, not `assert()` in production code.

```php
// ✅ CORRECT - @var annotation (zero runtime impact)
/** @var string $apiToken */
$apiToken = $this->env->get(['API_TOKEN']);

// ❌ WRONG - assert() in production code (runtime cost, can be disabled)
$apiToken = $this->env->get(['API_TOKEN']);
assert(is_string($apiToken));
```

### Imports

Always add `use` statements for vendor packages and project classes. Root namespace FQDNs acceptable (`\InvalidArgumentException`, `\RuntimeException`).

```php
// ✅ CORRECT
use Illuminate\Filesystem\Filesystem;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Storage;

$fs = new Filesystem();
throw new \InvalidArgumentException('Error');

// ❌ WRONG - inline FQDNs for non-root namespaces
$fs = new \Illuminate\Filesystem\Filesystem();
```

### Dependency Injection System

Use Laravel's Service Container via `app()` helper or constructor injection. Container uses reflection to auto-wire dependencies.

```php
// ✅ CORRECT - Constructor injection (preferred)
public function __construct(private readonly MyService $service) {}

// ✅ CORRECT - Resolve from container
$service = app(MyService::class);

// ❌ WRONG - Manual instantiation
$service = new MyService(new Dependency());
```

**Rule:** ALL object creation uses constructor injection or `app()` except DTOs, value objects, pure data structures.

**Container Access:** Constructor injection in production, direct instantiation in tests.

```php
// Production - Service Provider
class AppServiceProvider extends ServiceProvider {
    public function register(): void {
        $this->app->singleton(MyService::class, fn ($app) => new MyService(
            $app->make(Dependency::class)
        ));
    }
}

// Tests
$service = new MyService(mock(Dependency::class));
```

**Test Mocking:** Container supports `bind()` for mock instances:

```php
$this->app->bind(ConfigService::class, fn () => $mockConfig);
$command = $this->app->make(ToolInstallCommand::class);  // Gets mock
```

**Integration:** Entry point: artisan. Command registration: Service Providers. Services: Auto-injected via constructor.

### Layer Separation

**Command Layer:**

- Handle user interaction (input/output), orchestrate Services
- NO business logic (delegate to Services)
- NO duplicate orchestration (extract to shared Services)
- Responsible for console styling, error formatting, prompts
- Never invoke other commands (NO proxy commands)

**Service Layer:**

- Atomic, reusable functionality with NO console I/O
- Accept/return plain PHP data types
- Dependency-injected via constructor
- Handle business logic, external APIs, file operations
- Complex orchestration shared by Commands extracted to dedicated Services

**Service State:**

- Stateless: Pure operations, no internal state (validators, calculators, API clients)
- Stateful: Manage configuration/cached data (config loaders, file managers, repositories)
- Stateful services use lazy loading, explicit initialization via public methods (`load()`, `initialize()`), document requirements

**Console I/O:** Only Commands perform console I/O. Use Laravel's Artisan command methods for output. Services return exceptions/data for Commands to display. See 03-commands.mdc.

**Dependencies:**

- Commands depend on Services
- Services depend on Services/utilities
- All dependencies in constructor signatures
- NO circular dependencies

### Comments

**DocBlock:** Minimalist descriptions, parameters, return types for classes and functions.

**Comment structure:**

```
// ----
// {h1}
// ----

//
// {h2}
// ----

//
// {h3}

// {p}
```

Separate sections visually. One newline between headers/subheaders/paragraphs. No obvious comments. Remove comments when removing code.

### Quality Gates

ALWAYS run before completing task, fix all issues:

```bash
vendor/bin/rector $CHANGED_PHP_FILES   # Code improvements
vendor/bin/pint $CHANGED_PHP_FILES     # Fix style
vendor/bin/phpstan analyze $CHANGED_PHP_FILES_EXCEPT_TESTS  # NEVER run on tests/
```

PHPStan excluded from tests - tests focus on testing functionality over type compliance.
